From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dmayala <dmayala@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:47:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 0058] drm/a9_eink: log-only VCOM readback and PG trace after a
 recovered dip, HV-on rate limit, full_low by this update

Review 89d F6/F6b/F9/item 6.
- After a recovered wf-end dip (post-unlock path only, lockdep-asserted
  outside eng_lock, at most 64 per boot): fp9929a_read_vcom(); counters in a
  new rail_diag line diag_vcom; one log line with the settle reads' PG bit
  pattern, the vblank count/time at the settle entry and at the recovery
  (a9x_vblank, read-only), this update's mode, rect and clear, and VCOM; a
  mismatch is a warning only.
- Settle limit by a token bucket over HV-on time (pg_settle_rate_n 15 per
  pg_settle_rate_window_s 600, burst pg_settle_rate_burst 6; diag_rate skip
  counts the latches it causes); pg_settle_total_max default 30 -> 1000
  (sanity backstop). The per-session budget of 3 stays.
- diag_pg_end full_n/full_low classify by THIS update's rect (the engine's),
  not by the previous update's record.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
